WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.215
Every step we take in Power Query is written in a language called M.

2
00:00:05.215 --> 00:00:09.342
In this lesson we work with that code in the Advanced Editor.

3
00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:13.813
Here is the code for a second copy of our Financial Sample query.

4
00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.220
It only has two steps so far.

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.498
This copy has the raw data.

6
00:00:24.498 --> 00:00:28.661
The original Financial Sample query already has several cleaning steps.

7
00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:33.240
Instead of repeating them by hand, we can copy the code.

8
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.160
I open the Advanced Editor for the original query, select the cleaning steps, and copy them.

9
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.840
Then I paste them into the Advanced Editor of the second query, after its existing steps.

10
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.306
Notice the message at the bottom:

11
00:01:10.306 --> 00:01:11.459
Token Identifier expected.

12
00:01:11.459 --> 00:01:12.612
M is strict.

13
00:01:12.612 --> 00:01:17.992
Each step must end with a comma, except the last one, and the word

14
00:01:17.992 --> 00:01:22.220
in must be followed by the name of the final step.

15
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.893
So I correct the step names and make sure the line after in points

16
00:01:35.893 --> 00:01:37.840
to the last step of the query.

17
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.778
Another common message is Token Eof expected.

18
00:02:07.778 --> 00:02:13.335
It usually means there is extra text after the final step name, or a

19
00:02:13.335 --> 00:02:15.717
missing comma earlier in the code.

20
00:02:15.717 --> 00:02:20.480
Read the message, check the line it points to, and fix it.

21
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.326
When the code is correct, the editor says no syntax errors have been detected.

22
00:02:33.326 --> 00:02:38.271
Click Done, and the same cleaning steps are now applied to both queries.

23
00:02:38.271 --> 00:02:38.651
Tip:

24
00:02:38.651 --> 00:02:43.977
always copy the original code into a text file before you edit it, so

25
00:02:43.977 --> 00:02:46.640
you can go back if something breaks.

